  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nMany students say they have too much homework, and I agree that it can sometimes do more harm than good. After a full day of classes, students still have to spend three or four hours on assignments every night. This leaves them with very little time for sports, family, or sleep. Some homework is helpful because it lets students practice what they learned in class. But when teachers give busywork just to fill time, students get tired and stop caring about learning. Schools should set limits on homework so that it is useful and not overwhelming.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"excessive\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"excessive\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"excessive\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
